quran[6]{c,v,t}:
  8,70,"O (Esteemed) Prophet! Say to those prisoners (of war) in your custody: ‘If Allah finds any goodness in your heart, He will give you (something) better than what was taken away from you. And He will forgive you, and Allah is Most-Forgiving, All-Merciful.’"
  8,71,"And (Esteemed Prophet,) if they intend treachery against you, they have been treacherous with Allah before. But He has granted (you) power over them, and Allah is All-Knowing, All-Wise."
  8,72,"Indeed, those who believed, and migrated (to Medina), and strived with their possessions and their lives in the way of Allah, and those who sheltered and helped (them)—it is they who are guardians of one another. As for those who believed but did not migrate (for Allah), you have no obligation regarding their protection until they emigrate. Yet if they seek your help (against persecution) because of (their) religion, then helping them is your obligation, except against those people with whom you have a treaty (of non-interference). And Allah is All-Seeing of whatever you do."
  8,73,"As for the disbelievers, they are allies (and supporters) of one another. (O believers!) If you do not do the same (by becoming allies and supporters of one another), there will be (endless) persecution on the earth and great corruption."
  8,74,"As for those who believed, emigrated and struggled hard in the way of Allah, and those who provided (them) shelter and help, they are the ones who are the true believers. For them shall be forgiveness and a generous provision."
  8,75,"As for those who believed afterwards, emigrated and struggled hard alongside you, they are (also to be counted) among you. But the blood relatives are more entitled to (inherit from) one another, as ordained by Allah. Indeed, Allah is All-Knowing of everything."
